        "original_id": "d768f100-1d79-53ad-83d0-c4fd97ebe2a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Sydney to Melbourne Ultramarathon, Cliff Young Australian 6-day race\n- People: Cliff Young\n- Companies: Westfield Group\n- Places: Westfield Parramatta, Westfield Doncaster, Beech Forest, Victoria, Colac\n\nFacts:\n- In 1983, the inaugural Sydney to Melbourne Ultramarathon was sponsored by the Westfield Group, started at Westfield Parramatta shopping centre, and finished at Westfield Doncaster shopping centre, formerly called Doncaster Shoppingtown.\n- In May 1983, Cliff Young won the inaugural Sydney to Melbourne Westfield's Ultramarathon at age 61.\n- Cliff Young, born Albert Ernest Clifford Young, was an Australian potato farmer and athlete from Beech Forest, Victoria.\n- The Cliff Young Australian 6-day race began in 1983.\n- In 2004, the Cliff Young Australian 6-day race was renamed after Cliff Young, identified as a Colac farmer and the winner of the inaugural Sydney to Melbourne Westfield's Ultramarathon.\n- Westfield Parramatta has an approximate net leasable area of 137,407 square metres, contains 498 shops across five levels, and is Australia's fourth largest shopping centre by gross leasable area.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
